"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdocs=self.webpackChunkdocs||[]).push([[735],{57991:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"functions":[{"name":"CreateProgressBar","desc":"Builds a growth [ProgressBar] hosted in a fresh BillboardGui parented to\\n`parent` (normally the crop\'s attachment). The bar is offset slightly below\\nthe anchor so it sits at the base of the crop rather than through it.\\n\\nThe caller owns the result and must dispose of it with the module-local\\n`destroyProgressBar` helper, which destroys the BillboardGui as well \u2014 calling\\n`ProgressBar:Destroy()` alone leaks the billboard.","params":[{"name":"parent","desc":"Anchor for the billboard","lua_type":"Instance"},{"name":"cropName","desc":"Label shown on the bar","lua_type":"string"},{"name":"growthPercentage","desc":"Initial fill, 0..1","lua_type":"number"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"ProgressBar.ProgressBar"}],"function_type":"method","realm":["Client"],"source":{"line":504,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/Soil.luau"}},{"name":"new","desc":"Creates a Soil prop.\\n\\nSeeds the replica\'s `props` from `savedPropData` when the plot is being\\nrestored from a save (and with an empty crop list otherwise), then hands off\\nto [PropBaseClass.new] with the four harvest signals and the\\n`HarvestCrop`/`HarvestProduce` client allowlist.\\n\\nRealm-specific setup afterwards:\\n\\n- **Client** \u2014 allocates `crops`, starts the reconciliation loop\\n  ([Soil:_setupCropModels]), and re-pivots every crop when the prop is moved.\\n- **Server** \u2014 starts the tree produce timer ([Soil:_startProduceTimers]).\\n\\nBoth realms recompute [Soil:_setScaleModifier] on every `level` change.","params":[{"name":"propData","desc":"","lua_type":"PropData"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"Soil"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":549,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/Soil.luau"}},{"name":"_createProduceData","desc":"Mints one produce record for a tree: a fresh id, a random visual modifier, and\\na random scale scaled by the plot\'s [Soil:_setScaleModifier] multiplier.\\n\\n`forceCompletion` sets `creationTime` to 0 instead of now, which makes the\\nproduce read as fully ripe immediately \u2014 used by [Soil:GrowAllCrops].","params":[{"name":"forceCompletion","desc":"Spawn the produce already ripe","lua_type":"boolean?"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"CropTypes.ProduceData"}],"function_type":"method","realm":["Server"],"private":true,"source":{"line":631,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/Soil.luau"}},{"name":"_startProduceTimers","desc":"Starts the heartbeat that grows produce on mature trees. Runs for the life of\\nthe prop; owned by `self.cleanup`.\\n\\nEach tick, for every mature crop whose seed defines `cropTreeData`:\\n\\n1. Skip if the tree has already hit its lifetime `produceYield`.\\n2. If it carries no produce yet, spawn the first one.\\n3. Otherwise, spawn one more only once **all** existing produce has ripened,\\n   and only while the count is below the model\'s `CropAttachment` count.\\n\\nThe \\"all ripe before the next one\\" rule is what staggers a tree\'s produce\\ninstead of letting it fill every attachment at once, and `yields` is\\nincremented per spawn (never decremented) so `produceYield` is a lifetime cap\\nrather than a concurrent one.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","realm":["Server"],"private":true,"source":{"line":664,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/Soil.luau"}},{"name":"_setScaleModifier","desc":"Recomputes `self.scaleModifier` from the item\'s `props.sizeModifier`,\\noverridden by the current upgrade level\'s `props.sizeModifier` when the level\\ndefines one. Runs on construction and on every `level` change, on both realms.\\n\\nOnly affects crops and produce created *after* the change \u2014 existing crops\\nkeep the scale they were rolled with.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","private":true,"source":{"line":757,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/Soil.luau"}},{"name":"CreateNewCropEntry","desc":"Instantiates everything a newly replicated crop needs and returns the [Crop]\\nbookkeeping entry for it: the stage model, an Attachment on the soil model\\nthat prompts and UI hang off (raised 2 studs so prompts float above the crop),\\na growth [ProgressBar] when the crop is neither mature nor instantly grown,\\nand \u2014 for a mature tree \u2014 its produce mount points.\\n\\nReturns `nil` when the seed no longer resolves, the model has not been built\\nyet, or the offset falls outside the plot. Callers treat `nil` as \\"skip this\\nframe\\".\\n\\nThis only builds instances; the caller inserts the result into `self.crops`\\nand attaches the appropriate prompt.","params":[{"name":"cropData","desc":"Replicated crop record","lua_type":"CropTypes.SavedCropData"},{"name":"offset","desc":"Plot-relative position and rotation","lua_type":"CropTypes.CropOffset"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"Crop?"}],"function_type":"method","realm":["Client"],"source":{"line":796,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/Soil.luau"}},{"name":"_isOffsetWithinBounds","desc":"Whether a plot-relative offset falls inside the prop\'s bounding box footprint.\\n`offset.Y` is the **Z** axis in world space \u2014 offsets are 2D positions on the\\nsoil\'s top face, not vertical.\\n\\nReturns `false` when the prop has no bounding box yet.","params":[{"name":"offset","desc":"Plot-relative X/Z offset in studs","lua_type":"Vector2"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"boolean"}],"function_type":"method","private":true,"source":{"line":869,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/Soil.luau"}},{"name":"_isOffsetTooCloseToExistingCrops","desc":"Whether planting at `newOffset` would land within `BaseData.MIN_CROP_SPACING`\\nstuds of an existing crop. Reads the server replica, so this is server-only\\ndespite the plain-2D maths.","params":[{"name":"newOffset","desc":"Candidate plot-relative offset","lua_type":"Vector2"}],"returns":[{"desc":"`true` means the spot is blocked","lua_type":"boolean"}],"function_type":"method","realm":["Server"],"private":true,"source":{"line":898,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/Soil.luau"}},{"name":"AddSeed","desc":"Plants a seed at a plot-relative offset.\\n\\nSilently no-ops (with a warning only for an unknown seed) if the seed id is\\nnot a seed, the offset is outside the plot, or the spot is too close to an\\nexisting crop \u2014 the client is expected to have pre-checked with\\n[Soil:CanPlantAtOffset], so a rejection here means a stale preview or a\\ntampered request.\\n\\nRolls the crop\'s random rotation, `scale` (from `BaseData.CROP_SCALE_RANGE`,\\nmultiplied by the plot\'s `scaleModifier`) and visual modifier at plant time,\\nthen appends it to `props.crops` and republishes. Consuming the seed from the\\nplayer\'s inventory is the caller\'s responsibility.","params":[{"name":"seedItemId","desc":"Item id of the seed to plant","lua_type":"string"},{"name":"offset","desc":"Plot-relative X/Z offset in studs","lua_type":"Vector2"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","realm":["Server"],"source":{"line":940,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/Soil.luau"}},{"name":"CanPlantAtOffset","desc":"Whether a seed could be planted at `offset` right now \u2014 bounds and spacing\\ncombined. Exactly the checks [Soil:AddSeed] performs, exposed so a caller can\\ntest without attempting the plant.","params":[{"name":"offset","desc":"Plot-relative X/Z offset in studs","lua_type":"Vector2"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"boolean"}],"function_type":"method","realm":["Server"],"source":{"line":997,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/Soil.luau"}},{"name":"GetCropById","desc":"Looks up a planted crop\'s record by its `cropId`, reading whichever replica\\nthis realm owns. Returns `nil` if no crop matches \u2014 which is the normal result\\nafter the crop has been harvested.\\n\\nThe returned table is the live record, not a copy: mutating it and then\\nrepublishing `props` is how [Soil:InstantGrowCrop] works.","params":[{"name":"cropId","desc":"","lua_type":"string"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"CropTypes.SavedCropData?"}],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":1025,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/Soil.luau"}},{"name":"InstantGrowCrop","desc":"Marks a single crop `instantlyGrown`, pinning it to the `Mature` stage\\nregardless of elapsed time. Called after the player buys the `grow_crop`\\ndeveloper product from the crop\'s instant-grow prompt.\\n\\nWarns and no-ops if the crop id, its seed, or the seed\'s `maturityTime` cannot\\nbe resolved.","params":[{"name":"cropId","desc":"Crop to grow","lua_type":"string"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","realm":["Server"],"source":{"line":1063,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/Soil.luau"}},{"name":"GrowAllCrops","desc":"Instantly matures every crop on the plot. Backs the base\'s \\"Grow All\\" point.\\n\\nNormal crops are simply flagged `instantlyGrown`. Trees additionally have\\ntheir produce topped up to a full set of `CropAttachment` slots \u2014 existing\\nproduce has its `creationTime` zeroed so it reads as ripe, and missing slots\\nare filled with already-ripe produce \u2014 while still respecting the tree\'s\\nlifetime `produceYield`.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","realm":["Server"],"source":{"line":1112,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/Soil.luau"}},{"name":"HarvestAllCrops","desc":"Harvests everything harvestable on the plot in one pass and fires\\n`HarvestedBulk` with the collected items. Backs the base\'s \\"Harvest All\\"\\npoint.\\n\\nIterates backwards so removals do not disturb the traversal. Per crop:\\n\\n- **Trees** yield all their current produce and keep standing, with their\\n  produce list emptied; a tree that has exhausted its `produceYield` is\\n  removed from the plot at this point, since it can never bear again.\\n- **Normal crops** yield once and are removed, but only if mature or\\n  instantly grown \u2014 immature crops are left alone.\\n\\nUnlike [Soil:Harvest] this fires a single bulk signal rather than one\\n`Harvested` per crop, so the economy layer can credit the whole haul in one\\ntransaction.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","realm":["Server"],"source":{"line":1183,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/Soil.luau"}},{"name":"Harvest","desc":"Harvests one crop: removes it from `props.crops`, republishes, and fires\\n`Harvested` with the crop record and how long past maturity it was taken.\\nThat signal is the authoritative event the economy layer credits from.\\n\\nRefuses (with a warning) if the crop id is unknown or the crop is neither\\nmature nor instantly grown.\\n\\nThis is the unguarded internal path \u2014 it performs **no ownership check**.\\nClient-initiated harvests go through [Soil:HarvestCrop], which checks\\nownership and then delegates here.","params":[{"name":"cropId","desc":"Crop to harvest","lua_type":"string"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","realm":["Server"],"source":{"line":1273,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/Soil.luau"}},{"name":"HarvestCrop","desc":"Client-callable entry point for harvesting one crop \u2014 allow-listed in\\n`_allowedClientFunctions`, so it is reached via `DispatchRemoteEvent`, never\\ncalled directly.\\n\\nVerifies the caller owns the plot, resolves the crop, confirms it is\\nharvestable, then delegates to [Soil:Harvest]. A request for a crop that is\\nnot yet mature is dropped rather than errored \u2014 the intent is to surface a\\n\\"buy instant grow?\\" upsell there, which is not implemented yet.","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"The requesting client","lua_type":"Player"},{"name":"cropId","desc":"Crop to harvest; a missing id warns and no-ops","lua_type":"string?"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","realm":["Server"],"source":{"line":1341,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/Soil.luau"}},{"name":"HarvestProduce","desc":"Client-callable entry point for harvesting a single piece of tree produce \u2014\\nallow-listed in `_allowedClientFunctions`.\\n\\nVerifies ownership, locates the produce within its parent crop, removes it,\\nrepublishes and fires `HarvestedProduce`. The tree itself is untouched and\\nwill grow the slot back on its next produce tick; the tree is only ever\\nremoved by [Soil:HarvestAllCrops] once its `produceYield` is spent.","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"The requesting client","lua_type":"Player"},{"name":"produceId","desc":"Produce to take","lua_type":"string?"},{"name":"cropId","desc":"Tree the produce belongs to","lua_type":"string?"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","realm":["Server"],"source":{"line":1405,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/Soil.luau"}},{"name":"_calculateCropOffset","desc":"Converts a stored crop offset into a CFrame **in the soil part\'s local\\nspace** \u2014 translation on X/Z plus the crop\'s random yaw. Returns `nil` if the\\nmodel is not built or the offset is out of bounds.\\n\\nUse [Soil:_calculateCropOrigin] for a world-space result.","params":[{"name":"offset","desc":"","lua_type":"CropTypes.CropOffset"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"CFrame?"}],"function_type":"method","private":true,"source":{"line":1478,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/Soil.luau"}},{"name":"_calculateCropOrigin","desc":"World-space CFrame for a crop offset: [Soil:_calculateCropOffset] taken into\\nthe world space of the model\'s `Soil` part.\\n\\nOffsets are anchored to a part *named* `Soil` inside the model rather than to\\nthe model\'s `PrimaryPart`, so the plantable surface can be authored\\nindependently of the prop\'s pivot. Falls back to the `PrimaryPart` with a\\nwarning when that part is missing.","params":[{"name":"offset","desc":"","lua_type":"CropTypes.CropOffset"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"CFrame?"}],"function_type":"method","private":true,"source":{"line":1518,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/Soil.luau"}},{"name":"_recalculateCropPositions","desc":"Re-pivots every rendered crop after the plot itself moves. Wired to the\\ninherited `Moved` signal in the constructor.\\n\\nCrop offsets are stored relative to the soil part, so nothing in replicated\\ndata changes when the plot is relocated \u2014 only the derived world positions\\nneed refreshing.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","realm":["Client"],"private":true,"source":{"line":1552,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/Soil.luau"}},{"name":"_setupCropModels","desc":"Installs the RenderStepped loop that keeps the plot\'s visuals in sync with\\nreplicated crop data. This is the heart of the client half of Soil; it runs\\nfor the life of the prop and is owned by `self.cleanup`.\\n\\nIt first defines three prompt builders, chosen per crop by ownership and\\nstage:\\n\\n- `setAsGrowable` \u2014 owner, immature crop: an \\"Instant Grow\\" prompt that stages\\n  a `SOIL_PREPARE_INSTANT_GROW_PURCHASE` action and prompts the `grow_crop`\\n  product.\\n- `setAsHarvestable` \u2014 owner, mature crop or ripe produce: the harvest prompt,\\n  which participates in the hold-to-harvest sweep described on [Soil].\\n- `allowStealing` \u2014 non-owner, mature crop: a \\"Steal Crop\\" prompt behind a\\n  purchase. Inert while `ENABLE_STEALING` is `false`.\\n\\nEach RenderStep it then reconciles, per replicated crop:\\n\\n1. **Create** a [Crop] entry and prompt for anything not yet rendered.\\n2. **Advance the progress bar**, or destroy it once the crop is mature.\\n3. **Restage** \u2014 when the derived life stage differs from the rendered one,\\n   destroy the old model, build the new stage\'s model, re-scan tree\\n   attachments and re-pick the prompt.\\n4. **Rescale** otherwise, ramping the model toward its full size with growth.\\n5. **Sync produce** on mature trees: spawn a scaled clone of the crop part on\\n   a randomly chosen free attachment for each new produce, resize ripening\\n   produce every frame, add harvest prompts as produce matures, and destroy\\n   produce the server has removed.\\n\\nFinally it sweeps crops that vanished from replicated data \u2014 the client\'s cue\\nthat a harvest was accepted \u2014 firing the local `Harvested` signal, playing the\\nharvest particle and SFX, and destroying the model, bar, attachment and any\\nproduce.\\n\\nBecause state is rebuilt from the replica rather than mutated in place, a\\ndropped or reordered replication update self-corrects on the next frame.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","realm":["Client"],"private":true,"source":{"line":1615,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/Soil.luau"}}],"properties":[],"types":[{"name":"CropLifeStage","desc":"Growth stage of a planted crop. Derived from elapsed time on every read\\nrather than stored \u2014 see [Soil] for the thresholds. `Wilted` is only reachable\\nfor seeds that define a `harvestTime`; seeds without one stay `Mature`\\nindefinitely.","lua_type":"\\"Seed\\" | \\"Flower\\" | \\"Mature\\" | \\"Wilted\\"","source":{"line":147,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/Soil.luau"}},{"name":"Crop","desc":"Client-side view of one planted crop: the instances currently rendered for it,\\npaired with the server record they were built from. Lives in `Soil.crops` and\\nis reconciled against the replica every RenderStep. Server-side Soils have no\\n`Crop` objects at all.","fields":[{"name":"model","lua_type":"Model","desc":"The instantiated model for the current life stage"},{"name":"cropLifeStage","lua_type":"CropLifeStage","desc":"Stage the current model represents"},{"name":"cropData","lua_type":"CropTypes.SavedCropData","desc":"Reference to the replicated record"},{"name":"instantlyGrown","lua_type":"boolean","desc":"Pinned to Mature by an instant-grow purchase"},{"name":"position","lua_type":"CFrame","desc":"World origin, recomputed when the prop moves"},{"name":"progressBar","lua_type":"ProgressBar?","desc":"Growth bar; removed once mature"},{"name":"prompt","lua_type":"ProximityPrompt?","desc":"Instant-grow, harvest, or steal prompt"},{"name":"attachment","lua_type":"Attachment","desc":"Anchor on the soil model that prompts/UI hang off"},{"name":"cropAttachments","lua_type":"{ Attachment }","desc":"Produce mount points on a mature tree model"},{"name":"spawnedProduce","lua_type":"{ [Attachment]: { savedData: CropTypes.ProduceData, cropPart: BasePart, harvestPrompt: ProximityPrompt? } }","desc":"Produce currently rendered on this tree"},{"name":"isTree","lua_type":"boolean","desc":"Whether the seed defines `cropTreeData`"}],"source":{"line":169,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/Soil.luau"}},{"name":"GrowthData","desc":"Point-in-time snapshot of a crop\'s growth, computed from its `plantedAt` and\\nthe seed\'s timings. Recomputed on demand rather than cached, so it is always\\nconsistent with the server clock (`Workspace:GetServerTimeNow()`) on both\\nrealms.","fields":[{"name":"flowersAt","lua_type":"number","desc":"Server time the crop enters the Flower stage"},{"name":"maturesAt","lua_type":"number","desc":"Server time the crop becomes harvestable"},{"name":"wiltsAt","lua_type":"number?","desc":"Server time it wilts; nil when the seed never wilts"},{"name":"cropLifeStage","lua_type":"CropLifeStage","desc":"Stage as of the moment this was computed"}],"source":{"line":204,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/Soil.luau"}},{"name":"Soil","desc":"Instance shape of a Soil, on top of everything inherited from [PropBaseClass].\\n\\n`Harvested` fires on both realms but means slightly different things: on the\\nserver it fires from [Soil:Harvest] as the authoritative event that the\\neconomy layer credits the player from; on the client it fires from the\\nreconciliation pass whenever a crop disappears from replicated data, and is\\nused for local VFX/SFX only.","fields":[{"name":"clientReplica","lua_type":"ReplicaClient","desc":"Replica narrowed to `props: SavedSoilData` (client)"},{"name":"serverReplica","lua_type":"ReplicaServer","desc":"Replica narrowed to `props: SavedSoilData` (server)"},{"name":"Harvested","lua_type":"Signal","desc":"(soil, cropData, harvestTime) \u2014 a whole crop was taken"},{"name":"HarvestedBulk","lua_type":"Signal","desc":"(soil, { BulkCropDataItem }) \u2014 HarvestAllCrops finished"},{"name":"HarvestedProduce","lua_type":"Signal","desc":"(soil, produceData, cropId, harvestTime) \u2014 one tree produce was taken"},{"name":"HarvestReady","lua_type":"Signal","desc":"(soil, cropData) \u2014 a crop just became harvestable (client)"},{"name":"cleanup","lua_type":"Maid?","desc":"Owns every connection made by this Soil"},{"name":"crops","lua_type":"{ Crop }?","desc":"Rendered crops (client only)"},{"name":"scaleModifier","lua_type":"number","desc":"Multiplier applied to new crop and produce scale"}],"source":{"line":232,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/Soil.luau"}}],"name":"Soil","desc":"The farming plot prop. A Soil is a rectangular patch that holds any number of\\nindependently planted crops, each at its own offset within the patch. It\\nextends [PropBaseClass] and is also re-exported unchanged as `BiggerSoil` \u2014\\nthe two differ only in item data (a larger model and a larger\\n`props.sizeModifier`), not in behaviour.\\n\\n### Crop lifecycle\\n\\nEvery planted crop is a [SavedCropData] record inside the prop\'s persisted\\n`props.crops` list. It carries the seed item id, the server timestamp it was\\nplanted at, a plot-relative `offset` (X/Y studs plus a random yaw), a random\\n`scale` and a random visual `modifier`. From `plantedAt` plus the seed\'s\\n`floweringTime`/`maturityTime`/`harvestTime` the class derives a\\n[GrowthData] snapshot every frame \u2014 no growth state is stored, so growth\\ncontinues while the owner is offline and needs no catch-up pass.\\n\\nLife stages run `Seed` \u2192 `Flower` \u2192 `Mature` \u2192 `Wilted`, each with its own\\nmodel in `Assets.Crops.<CropName>`. A crop marked `instantlyGrown` (via the\\ndeveloper-product instant-grow prompt) is pinned to `Mature` and skips the\\ntimers entirely.\\n\\n### Trees and produce\\n\\nSeeds whose data carries `cropTreeData` grow into *trees*, which are never\\nharvested themselves. Instead a mature tree accumulates [ProduceData]\\nentries on a server timer, one per `produceGrowTime`, up to the number of\\n`CropAttachment` points on its mature model and up to an optional lifetime\\n`produceYield`. Each produce is rendered as a clone of the crop\'s `Crop` part\\npinned to a free attachment, scaled from `MINIMUM_SCALE` up to full size as\\nit ripens, and gets its own harvest prompt on maturity. Harvesting a tree\'s\\nproduce leaves the tree standing; only a tree that has exhausted its\\n`produceYield` is removed.\\n\\n### Placement rules\\n\\nPlanting is validated on the server: the offset must sit inside the prop\'s\\nbounding box ([Soil:_isOffsetWithinBounds]) and at least\\n`BaseData.MIN_CROP_SPACING` studs away from every existing crop\\n([Soil:_isOffsetTooCloseToExistingCrops]). Together these are exposed as\\n[Soil:CanPlantAtOffset] so the client\'s placement preview can refuse before\\nround-tripping.\\n\\n### Scale modifiers\\n\\nThe prop\'s `scaleModifier` multiplies the random scale given to new crops and\\nproduce. It comes from the item\'s `props.sizeModifier`, overridden by the\\ncurrent upgrade level\'s `props.sizeModifier` when present, and is recomputed\\nwhenever the replica\'s `level` changes \u2014 so upgrading a plot grows the things\\nplanted in it from then on.\\n\\n### Realms\\n\\nThe server owns all crop state and is the only side that mutates\\n`props.crops`. The client owns models, progress bars and prompts, rebuilt\\nfrom the replica in a single RenderStepped reconciliation pass\\n([Soil:_setupCropModels]) that creates, restages, rescales and destroys crop\\nmodels to match server data. Harvesting is client-initiated through\\n`DispatchRemoteEvent`, and only `HarvestCrop` and `HarvestProduce` are\\nallow-listed.\\n\\n### Harvest input\\n\\nCrops are harvested by holding `BaseData.HARVEST_KEY` (or the on-screen\\nbutton on touch devices) and walking through them: while held, any prompt\\nthat becomes visible auto-triggers, throttled to one harvest per\\n`HARVEST_DELAY`. The hold state is module-level and shared by every Soil in\\nthe world, so a single keypress sweeps a whole farm. Triggering a prompt\\ndirectly still works as a single-crop fallback.\\n\\nStealing other players\' crops is fully implemented behind the module-level\\n`ENABLE_STEALING` constant, which is `false`; with it off, non-owners get no\\nprompts at all.\\n\\nGated by [FeatureFlags].BaseEnabled \u2014 disabled by default; per-project forks\\nenable it deliberately.\\n\\nCopyright (c) 2026 firebit. All rights reserved.\\nfirebit/murder-escape - proprietary and confidential.","tags":["dormant"],"source":{"line":84,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/Soil.luau"}}')}}]);